#### Variation A: Shared step definitions with fixture injection

For languages that support dependency injection in test fixtures (Python pytest, C# DI containers), step definitions can be shared across adapters with the adapter instance injected via a fixture or factory:

```python
# conftest.py — parameterized adapter fixture
@pytest.fixture(params=["redis", "memcached", "memory"])
def cache_adapter(request):
    if request.param == "redis":
        return RedisCache(host="localhost", port=6379)
    elif request.param == "memcached":
        return MemcachedCache(host="localhost", port=11211)
    else:
        return InMemoryCache()
```

This variation reduces code duplication but makes failure attribution slightly less direct — the test report must clearly identify which parameterized instance failed.

